llvmnet port of LLVM's OpenMP runtime (openmp/runtime) 22.1.8 for the dotnet64-v2 ABI; applied by
scripts/build-portable-openmp.sh with patch -p1. The portable target is a Linux userland without an architecture
macro, so KMP_OS_LINUX is set from __LLVMNET_PORTABLE__ and a new architecture, KMP_ARCH_LLVMNET, selects the
generic C code: the C __kmp_invoke_microtask, builtin atomics, __sync_synchronize barriers, no processor
affinity (there is none on managed threads) and no assembly. Worker stacks default to 4 MB as on x86-64, and a
microtask with more arguments than the C invoker's cases receives the argument array through the thunk llvmnet's
linker generates for it.

